{
  "id": "lagrange-point-1991",
  "kind": "game",
  "title": "Lagrange Point",
  "subtitle": "Konami · Nintendo Entertainment System",
  "summary": "Lagrange Point is Konami's science-fiction role-playing game for the Famicom, set among artificial space colonies. A biological disaster cuts off communication with Land-2, and a research expedition arrives to investigate. Its pilot Gene survives an attack and begins searching for the people who might explain what happened. The setting replaces a familiar fantasy kingdom with settlements built to sustain human life away from Earth. Moving between their inhabitants and dangerous surroundings gives the emergency a human scale before the larger conflict becomes clear.",
  "body": [
    "Lagrange Point is Konami's science-fiction role-playing game for the Famicom, set among artificial space colonies. A biological disaster cuts off communication with Land-2, and a research expedition arrives to investigate. Its pilot Gene survives an attack and begins searching for the people who might explain what happened. The setting replaces a familiar fantasy kingdom with settlements built to sustain human life away from Earth. Moving between their inhabitants and dangerous surroundings gives the emergency a human scale before the larger conflict becomes clear.",
    "The Isis Cluster contains two artificial biospheres and a satellite, placing the journey within a connected human settlement rather than an unexplored distant planet. Gene's damaged expedition leaves him dependent on the people and information found after his arrival. The search for a researcher from the Bio Research Lab gives the early investigation a concrete destination. The game uses a role-playing adventure's gradual discovery of places and companions to reveal how a planned new home has become a place threatened by its own catastrophe.",
    "Konami placed its VRC7 chip inside the cartridge, giving the music FM synthesis capabilities beyond the Famicom's ordinary sound hardware. That makes the soundtrack an important part of the game's technological identity as well as its atmosphere. The original release remained in Japan; an unofficial English translation followed in 2014. Its title refers to positions in space where the relationship between two large bodies can keep a third in a stable configuration. Here, that idea becomes the location of a human community whose stability has been violently disturbed."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "A disaster beyond Earth",
    "Follow the surviving accounts",
    "A cartridge with another musical voice"
  ],
